 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Most people go 50 50 down the aisle, but some couples ask each other's families to chip in according to each family's means. It depends on the couple. Then it' his family saying yes with no string attached, and yours cover any overages. It's fair to him, since you didn't ask his family. Not really, it' simple and fair. Some people would be offended if you made them contribute without asking. Then you could ask his parents again, once it' clear it's serious, and say you'd like to keep the cost down for both families. Many people would then agree. Good plan. Just make sure he does it in person, not on the phone.",
